  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material as the subject of the joke",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'when each letter is a mental disorder' as the implied subject of the pun. The meme invites the user to imagine themselves as the one making the absurd claim or as the one who would find the joke funny, thereby projecting their own perspective onto the textual material. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the humor relies on the user's participation in the joke by interpreting the text in a specific, self-referential way. The user is not projected onto a specific visual material or scene, but rather onto the conceptual framework of the text, which requires the user to engage with the idea that mental disorders are being trivialized through a childish game.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
